From fd3f9787559480d8726a50c75b171429f2a17a12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:51:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] seccomp: look up filter libraries in lib64 on 64-bit builds

Commit c4b26050 ("support the 64-bit seccomp filter path") meant to
switch the lib64 path selection from __aarch64__ to __LP64__ but wrote
__LP__, which no compiler defines.  Every 64-bit build therefore looks
for /system/lib/seccomp/lib<name>_filter.z.so while the filters are
installed to /system/lib64/seccomp.

With build_seccomp on, the lookup always fails: appspawn exits 0x7f in
its preload hook ("get filter name failed", then "Failed to set
APPSPAWN seccomp filter and exit"), init restarts it until the
critical-service limit reboots the device, and every sa_main service
exits the same way through init's SetSeccompPolicy.

Use __LP64__ as the commit intended.

Change-Id: I7b2ce95d982e8fc7ff5b817b37dad72d242d1351
Signed-off-by: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
---
 services/modules/seccomp/seccomp_policy.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/modules/seccomp/seccomp_policy.c b/services/modules/seccomp/seccomp_policy.c
index ebee99b0..b3c2d177 100644
--- a/services/modules/seccomp/seccomp_policy.c
+++ b/services/modules/seccomp/seccomp_policy.c
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 #define SECCOMP_SET_MODE_FILTER  (1)
 #endif
 
-#ifdef __LP__
+#ifdef __LP64__
 #define FILTER_LIB_PATH_FORMAT "lib64/seccomp/lib%s_filter.z.so"
 #define FILTER_LIB_PATH_PART "lib64/seccomp/lib"
 #else
-- 
2.50.1

